#!/usr/bin/python3
"""qubes-plymouth-scramble: scrambled digit keys for the Qubes OS disk password prompt.

Stock Plymouth reads keys through XKB when vconsole.conf names an XKB layout. This tool
installs a dracut module whose boot hook writes a new random digit layout into the
initramfs (RAM) on every boot and hands the map to a keypad overlay appended to the image's
copy of the stock qubes-dark theme. Plymouth itself is not modified.

Commands (run as root in dom0; install and uninstall list every change and ask first):
  install        apply the configuration: generate the dracut module, then build, validate
                 and switch to new initramfs images for the running kernel and every kernel
                 whose image has the hook (enabled = no keeps only this tool in the module
                 directory, which dracut then skips, and builds stock images)
  uninstall      remove the dracut module (with this tool), its link and the configuration,
                 then switch to stock images
  status         show what is installed
  validate-tree  check a staged or unpacked initramfs (used by the dracut module)
"""

